{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 14,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Israel, return to the LORD thy God; for thou hast fallen by thy iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take with you words, and turn to the LORD: say to him, Take away all iniquity, and receive ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " graciously: so will we render the calves of our lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ashur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses: neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ye are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our gods: for in thee the fatherless findeth mercy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely: for my anger is turned away from him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will be as the dew to Israel: he shall grow as the lily and cast forth his roots as Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His branches shall spread, and his beauty shall be as the olive-tree, and his smell as Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that dwell under his shade shall return; they shall revive ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the corn, and grow as the vine: the scent of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the wine of Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", What have I to do any more with idols? I have heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and observed him: I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like a green fir-tree. From me is thy fruit found.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.14.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.14.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise, and he shall understand these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? prudent, and he shall know them? for the ways of the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right, and the just shall walk in them: but the transgressors shall fall in them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
